    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "66271828_b2a7ce50",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 475,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-13T11:26:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`device_initcall_sync()` is the first initcall level to run after KVM has initialised (since iirc KVM is initialised via `module_init()` which equates to `device_initcall()` when it is built-in). Keeping the window between init failure and clearing of pvmfw as small as possible seems like a sensible thing to do.\n\nI\u0027m a bit nervous if we\u0027re racing against unpacking the initramfs, as that seems dodgy regardless of which initcall level we\u0027re using. Can we not block on that completing instead?",
      "parentUuid": "69ec7d18_958d76bf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 475,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 475,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "3a9d87b5db75fb5e799d109855e813d4f8bcdf86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
